{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>The enemy said, etc.</b> The reason for the repetition of these words — which are themselves the same as what was said at the beginning of the song, ״מַרְכְּבוֹת פַּרְעֹה וְחֵילוֹ יָרָה בַיָּם״ etc. — is to sing about the manner of the order of the deed that HaShem contrived in the work of the sea for Israel as a miracle. And HaShem commanded that the miracle stand in its usual course and in its customary way for the enemy, for through this he erred and thought to pursue, thinking he would overtake and divide the spoil — for without this he would not have pursued by way of the sea, and they would not have been endangered by him." "<b>I will divide the spoil.</b> See, the wicked one planned to do three things — all three equal, and it is to plunder all their spoil, which is his saying ״אֲחַלֵּק שָׁלָל״. The second, that he would take them as slaves as at first, which is his saying <b>תִּמְלָאֵמוֹ נַפְשִׁי</b> — meaning, my soul will be filled from them when I return to subjugate them as slaves. Also he hinted that he would further do his will with them in affliction more than what had already passed. The third, to kill Moses and Aaron and their elders and their nobles, which is his saying <b>אָרִיק חַרְבִּי</b> etc. And his saying <b>תּוֹרִישֵׁמוֹ יָדִי</b> intends in accordance with what our Sages of blessed memory said (Shemot Rabbah 1:31) on the verse (Exodus 2:15) ״וַיְבַקֵּשׁ לַהֲרֹג אֶת מֹשֶׁה״ — that he sought to kill him with the sword but it did not prevail against him, etc. And this is what Moses said (Exodus 18:4): ״וַיַּצִּלֵנִי מֵחֶרֶב פַּרְעֹה״. Therefore the enemy said ״תּוֹרִישֵׁמוֹ יָדִי״ — for his hand would achieve what it had not achieved before."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:29.296728371Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}